        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1cfa8c66-ac04-5096-997c-a32c87b2a8dd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Yang Yun-ho, Choi Yeung-Eui\n- Works: Libera Me, Fighter in the Wind, Holiday, Rainbow Eyes, Grand Prix, Karate Baka Ichidai\n- Events: 2005 Grand Bell Awards, World War II\n- Places: South Korea, Japan\n\nFacts:\n- After World War II, Choi Yeung-Eui went to Japan intending to become a fighter pilot, according to the fictionalized account in the Japanese book Karate Baka Ichidai.\n- Fighter in the Wind is a 2004 South Korean film.\n- Fighter in the Wind is based on the Japanese book Karate Baka Ichidai.\n- Yang Yun-ho directed Libera Me in 2000.\n- Yang Yun-ho directed Fighter in the Wind in 2004.\n- Yang Yun-ho received a Best Adapted Screenplay nomination at the 2005 Grand Bell Awards for Fighter in the Wind.\n- Yang Yun-ho directed Holiday in 2006.\n- Yang Yun-ho directed Rainbow Eyes in 2007.\n- Yang Yun-ho directed Grand Prix in 2010.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
